  "notes": "Digitized from the Kodak E-4042 datasheet of July 2008. Kodak: \"vivid color, neutral tone scale, and excellent flesh tones\", \"for making color prints from digital camera files or files from scanned negatives\" in digital printers; named for optical printing by the first sheets of today's Portra 400 (E-4050, 2010) and Portra 160 (E-4051, 2011); since replaced by ENDURA Premier. Status A curves for a 0.5 s sensitometric exposure; the enlarger is the same stand-in as ENDURA Premier's. No granularity and no MTF on the sheet. R, G and B by D-max, the order the sheet's labels stand in at the curves' ends.",
